  "comment": "## Middleware built and tested\n\nImplemented the full RFID middleware in `clients/ROH/middleware/`.\n\n### What was built:\n- **Project setup:** Python package with `pyproject.toml`, httpx dependency, venv\n- **Abstract reader interface** (`reader.py`): `RFIDReader` ABC with `connect()`, `disconnect()`, `read_tags()` async iterator\n- **Mock reader** (`reader.py`): Simulates dual-antenna reads with realistic timing for dev/testing without hardware\n- **Direction detection** (`processor.py`): Dual-antenna sequencing — inner-first = out, outer-first = in, 3s window. Single-antenna fallback marked \"uncertain\"\n- **Tag debouncing** (`processor.py`): Configurable window (default 10s) suppresses rapid re-reads\n- **Event dispatcher** (`dispatcher.py`): POSTs to backend `/api/events` via httpx with error handling\n- **Main entry point** (`main.py`): asyncio event loop, signal handling, auto-reconnect with exponential backoff\n- **Config** (`config.py`): All settings configurable via environment variables\n- **8 unit tests** — all passing (direction detection + debouncing)\n\n### Files created:\n```\nmiddleware/\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── roh_middleware/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── config.py\n│   ├── reader.py\n│   ├── processor.py\n│   ├── dispatcher.py\n│   └── main.py\n└── tests/\n    ├── __init__.py\n    └── test_processor.py\n```\n\n### Note on RFID reader SDK:\nThe task description notes \"Blocked until: RFID reader model confirmed by client.\" The abstract `RFIDReader` interface is ready — when the reader model is confirmed, we just add a new implementation class (e.g., `ImpinjReader`) alongside the existing `MockReader`. No architecture changes needed.\n\nTo run with mock reader: `ROH_READER_TYPE=mock python -m roh_middleware.main`"
